BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 679.0 Tm (The volume contains boot area, superblock, inode bitmap, zone bitmap, inode table and data) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 662.0 Tm (zones. The superblock identifies version-dependent magic, inode count, zone count, bitmap) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 645.0 Tm (block counts, first data zone, log-zone size and size limits. MINIX V1 inodes use smaller) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 628.0 Tm (zone addresses than later revisions, and V3 uses a distinct superblock representation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 599.0 Tm (Zones are the units through which file data is allocated, while block I/O can be a separate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 582.0 Tm (granularity. Direct pointers address initial zones, with single and double indirect) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 565.0 Tm (mappings extending larger files. Linux kernel source demonstrates separate handling for V1,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 548.0 Tm (V2 and V3 geometry and guards against unsupported zone-size combinations.) Tj ET
