BT /F2 14 Tf 0.01 0.43 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 50 713.0 Tm (INTEGRITY AND RECOVERY) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 679.0 Tm (Traditional MINIX filesystems do not have a full metadata journal or native copy-on-write) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 662.0 Tm (snapshots. Offline checks compare inode and zone bitmaps with the reachable directory graph) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 645.0 Tm (and inode pointers. A crash may leave a bitmap entry set for an unreachable zone, or an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 628.0 Tm (inode referencing a zone not marked allocated. Both directions must be checked before any) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 611.0 Tm (repair decision.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 582.0 Tm (The superblock magic is only the first stage of format validation. A safe reader then) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 565.0 Tm (verifies bitmap capacity, first data zone, inode bounds and indirect-pointer ranges, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 548.0 Tm (refuses unsupported feature combinations. Guessing format based on the filename or copying) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 531.0 Tm (only the superblock to repair an image is unsafe.) Tj ET
