BT /F2 14 Tf 0.01 0.43 0.49 rg 1 0 0 1 50 713.0 Tm (DESIGN RATIONALE AND LIMITATIONS) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 679.0 Tm (MINIX optimised pedagogical clarity and compact code rather than massive filesystem size or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 662.0 Tm (high-concurrency workloads. Its simple separation between inode and zone bitmaps makes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 645.0 Tm (allocation easy to explain and implement. This is historically important in the development) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 628.0 Tm (of educational and early Linux systems.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 599.0 Tm (The price was restricted name lengths, file sizes and lack of journalling. Version-specific) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 582.0 Tm (constraints matter more than a single aggregate MINIX capacity figure. Newer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 565.0 Tm (implementations sometimes interpret the same concepts with more robust validation, but that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 548.0 Tm (should not be projected back onto original MINIX V1 media.) Tj ET
